  "prefLabel": "Env-Sw 2102.22 Utility/transportation project",
  "recordType": "rule-section",
  "ruleText": "Env-Sw 2102.22 “Utility/transportation project” means:\n\n(a) A minor or major project undertaken by a utility company or public authority or pursuant to a contract with a utility company or public authority to install, repair, replace, or decommission a private or public utility system, or portion thereof, at locations where the responsible utility company or public authority holds such rights of access, and includes the installation, repair, replacement, and decommissioning of the following:\n\n(1) Sanitary sewerage, water, or drainage systems, and related appurtenances;\n\n(2) Steam lines and related appurtenances;\n\n(3) Natural gas pipelines and related appurtenances; and\n\n(4) Above-ground or underground electric, telephone, telecommunication cables or other conduits, and related appurtenances;\n\n(b) A minor or major project undertaken by a public authority or pursuant to a contract with a public authority to construct, reconstruct, or repair all or a portion of a public way such as a street, road, or highway; or\n\n(c) A minor or major project undertaken to repair, restore, or remove railroad tracks.\n\nSource. #12605, eff 9-1-18 (formerly Env-Sw 2102.12)",
  "source": "https://github.com/GraniteState/adm-rules-data/blob/1c92d82e0f03a582ca5b7a578588edf38de2318e/raw/2026-11-15/state_agencies/env-sw2100.html"
}
